{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "4736f250-0749-8af7-89ae-d894ffd54927",
  "created_at": "2026-02-05T09:58:17-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Anthony Santoro",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Kevin Sousa",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T09:56:30-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Kevin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T09:56:32-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good morning, Kevin. My name is Anthony Santoro. Let me explain what I'm calling about. I've been saving my recycling for a couple of weeks now, and I realized I'm not sure what's allowed anymore."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T09:56:42-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure, no problem. What are you wondering about?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T09:56:45-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, first, pizza boxes. I had a pizza last weekend, and the box has some grease on the bottom. Does that go in the bin?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T09:56:52-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, pizza boxes. Generally, if it's greasy or has food stuck to it, that's a trash item. A clean cardboard lid, you can tear that off and recycle it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T09:57:00-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I see. So tear off the clean part. And what about glass? Jars, mostly, from sauce and pickles."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T09:57:06-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Glass jars and bottles are fine, just rinse them out. Lids can go on or off, but empty them first."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T09:57:12-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good. And then the plastic clamshells, the kind that strawberries and salad come in. Those are the third thing."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T09:57:18-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, those clear clamshell containers, rinsed, usually go in with the plastics. I'm jotting that down so I don't skip anything. Pizza, tear the clean part. Glass, rinsed. Clamshells, rinsed."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T09:57:27-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's right. Now, when is my next pickup? I don't have the calendar in front of me."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T09:57:32-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'd need your street to look at your route, but if you don't want to give an address, I can tell you the schedule is by area. Do you want to give me the street?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T09:57:42-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'd rather not give it over the phone. I'll look at the calendar on the refrigerator. Is it the same day as trash, usually?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T09:57:49-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Recycling is typically the same day as trash, alternating weeks. Check the calendar for the week marked for recycling."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T09:57:55-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Fine, I'll do that. One more thing, unrelated. There's a secondhand piano for sale a few doors down, and I'm eyeing it. I'm just wondering what happens with the big items if I ever had to get rid of one."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T09:58:06-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Bulky items usually need to be scheduled separately. Call us back if it comes to that and we can go over it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T09:58:13-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Very good. Thank you, Kevin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T09:58:15-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome. Take care."
    }
  ],
